    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="1032" n="896" xml:id="pg896"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/705: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kreeck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-17T16:00:00-03:50">September 17, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 18—2:37 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>88. Minister for Foreign Affairs asks that I officially notify the United States
                    Government that the Paraguayan Government accepts with great pleasure the good
                    offices tendered by the United States in its note of September 14th,<anchor
                        n="67" xml:id="d744-f1"/> and that the official note of acceptance will
                        follow.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d744-f2"/> Acceptances have been given to the
                    other neutral countries with the exception of Uruguay which until fifteenth has
                    not offered to continue its good offices.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kreeck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d744-f1" n="67" xml:id="d744-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 42, September 13, 1 p.m., to the Minister in Paraguay, <ref
                        target="#pg892">p. 892</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d744-f2" n="68" xml:id="d744-f2-content">
                <p>Transmitted to the Department by the Minister as an enclosure to his despatch No.
                    916, September 23; neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
